{
  "id": "law_of_cosines",
  "title": "Law of Cosines",
  "description": "One side of a triangle when the opposite angle and two sides are known. The \"Law of Cosines\" can be used to calculate one side of a triangle when the angle opposite and the other two sides are known.",
  "type": "datatable",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "content": "Calculate side c of a triangle using the Law of Cosines formula: c = √(a² + b² - 2ab·cos(C))",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "side_a",
          "label": "Side a",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1,
          "unit": "m"
        },
        {
          "id": "side_b",
          "label": "Side b",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 1.3,
          "unit": "m"
        },
        {
          "id": "angle_c",
          "label": "Angle C",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 60,
          "unit": "degrees"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "side_c",
          "label": "Side c",
          "formula": "sqrt(inputs.side_a^2 + inputs.side_b^2 - 2*inputs.side_a*inputs.side_b*cos(inputs.angle_c*pi/180))",
          "unit": "m",
          "format": "decimal"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "datatable",
      "headers": [
        "Side a (m)",
        "Side b (m)",
        "Angle C (degrees)",
        "Side c (m)"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          1,
          1.3,
          60,
          "=sqrt(1^2 + 1.3^2 - 2*1*1.3*cos(60*pi/180))"
        ],
        [
          2,
          2.5,
          45,
          "=sqrt(2^2 + 2.5^2 - 2*2*2.5*cos(45*pi/180))"
        ],
        [
          3,
          3.5,
          90,
          "=sqrt(3^2 + 3.5^2 - 2*3*3.5*cos(90*pi/180))"
        ],
        [
          1.5,
          2,
          30,
          "=sqrt(1.5^2 + 2^2 - 2*1.5*2*cos(30*pi/180))"
        ],
        [
          2.5,
          3,
          120,
          "=sqrt(2.5^2 + 3^2 - 2*2.5*3*cos(120*pi/180))"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Formula\n\nThe Law of Cosines states:\n\n**c² = a² + b² - 2ab·cos(C)**\n\nWhere:\n- **a, b, c** = length of triangle sides (m, ft, etc.)\n- **C** = angle opposite side c (degrees)\n\n## Example\n\nIf side a = 1 m, side b = 1.3 m, and angle C = 60 degrees:\n\nc = √(1² + 1.3² - 2(1)(1.3)cos(60°))\nc = √(1 + 1.69 - 2.6 × 0.5)\nc = √(1.59) ≈ 1.26 m"
    }
  ]
}